      "writtenOn": "2021-11-05T22:27:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I tried that method which uses single quote and should be good for things like in ninja rules:\n\ncd output_directory \u0026\u0026 rm -rf output_file \u0026\u0026 some_command \u0027escaped args\u0027\n\nif we enforce /bin/bash, the upper command becomes:\n\ncd output_directory \u0026\u0026 rm -rf output_file \u0026\u0026 /bin/bash -c \u0027some_command \u0027escaped_args\u0027\u0027, \n\nwhich is not right and the part of \u003csome_command \u0027escaped_args\u0027\u003e in single quote should be escaped again which is quite confusing when handling the template content of python programs.\n\nSo I used double quote instead of single quote and the command looks like:\n\ncd output_directory \u0026\u0026 rm -rf output_file \u0026\u0026 /bin/bash -c \u0027echo \"escaped content for double quote\" \u0027\n\nThe function escapeCommandlineArgument escapes string for being used in double quote.",
